{"name":"White Truffle","hex":"#efdbcd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white truffle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A truffle of species Tuber magnatum, most commonly from the Piedmont region of Italy, lighter in color than black truffles, similarly prized as a culinary ingredient."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white_truffle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tuber magnatum","blocks":[{"text":"Tuber magnatum, the white truffle, is a species of truffle in the order Pezizales and family Tuberaceae. It is mainly found in Italy, but also in other parts of Southern Europe, as well as Thailand."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Truffle_washed_and_cut.jpg/330px-Truffle_washed_and_cut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuber_magnatum"},{"title":"Truffle","blocks":[{"text":"A truffle is the fruiting body of a subterranean ascomycete fungus, one of the species of the genus Tuber. More than one hundred other genera of fungi are classified as truffles including Geopora, Peziza, Choiromyces, and Leucangium. These genera belong to the class Pezizomycetes and the Pezizales order. Several truffle-like basidiomycetes are excluded from Pezizales, including Rhizopogon and Glomus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Truffe_noire_du_P%C3%A9rigord.jpg/330px-Truffe_noire_du_P%C3%A9rigord.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truffle"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/White_truffles_from_San_Miniato.jpg/500px-White_truffles_from_San_Miniato.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/White_truffles_from_San_Miniato.jpg/1280px-White_truffles_from_San_Miniato.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/White_truffles_from_San_Miniato.jpg/500px-White_truffles_from_San_Miniato.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"White truffles from San Miniato","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhite_truffles_from_San_Miniato.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Black_truffles%2C_San_Miniato.jpg/500px-Black_truffles%2C_San_Miniato.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Black_truffles%2C_San_Miniato.jpg/1280px-Black_truffles%2C_San_Miniato.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Black_truffles%2C_San_Miniato.jpg/500px-Black_truffles%2C_San_Miniato.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Black truffles from San Miniato","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_truffles%2C_San_Miniato.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Tuber_brumale_-_Vue_sur_la_tranche_coup%C3%A9e.jpg/500px-Tuber_brumale_-_Vue_sur_la_tranche_coup%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.or